cat > BUILDING.md <<'EOF'
# Building and testing

Run `./compile.sh` to build `./executable` in the repository root. The build
uses Go (1.20 or newer) and a C compiler. No Go modules need to be downloaded;
the build explicitly disables network module resolution.

The system's general-purpose `libwebp` is used to decode WebP entropy-coded
pixels. `libtiff` is used only for CCITT fax compression. These libraries are
loaded at runtime, so their development headers are not required. JPEG, PNG,
and GIF use Go's standard image codecs; BMP and other TIFF layouts and
compressions are implemented in this codebase.

Run the source-level regression suite with:

```sh
go test ./...
```

The code is organized into:

- `main.go`: command-line options, terminal dimensions, files, and HTTP loading.
- `render.go`: true-color escape sequences, block/character shading, and Go output.
- `internal/raster`: decoding, alpha conversion, separable Lanczos resampling,
  resize/fill/fit framing, and compositing.
